#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059730 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059543 :question/id #uuid "1ab8245a-39fb-5633-b5ff-865ab17dbfb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4323" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 0,-0.4,11 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,5,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 2+(-0.4)\\cdot 5+11\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0-2+22 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68abb4f0-c532-5cb6-882c-dacfe6a945dc" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050173 :topic/math-academy-id 1166 :topic/title "Three-Dimensional Vectors in Component Form"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0888ddef-8bdd-5f2a-9651-377e2d59b4fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266221} {:answer/id #uuid "65cbccca-5647-533f-9957-61401f6703fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267047} {:answer/id #uuid "73c31d02-3131-57b8-a4b6-76ae1cf00f68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267162} {:answer/id #uuid "93171610-1482-5b05-a8ec-52bcb035bb11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267460} {:answer/id #uuid "bb720482-33bd-5d46-b376-8816f86a87bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93171610-1482-5b05-a8ec-52bcb035bb11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267460} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae56222c-36e1-52f9-b169-6a33e59a6f02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268719}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "299fd51e-9aaf-5d57-966c-4d85ff141159" :question/math-academy-id "q-1340" :question/problem "Let $u=⟨-3,2⟩$ and $v=⟨7,9⟩.$ Find $u\\cdot v.$" :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 7+2\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =-21+18 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0a5a756-722b-5967-81a3-734cefc8ec24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056545} {:answer/id #uuid "c1770900-f1ca-564e-8acd-cbff21e07109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056546} {:answer/id #uuid "f1243975-2701-5e3b-9ead-25c1860cda0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056547} {:answer/id #uuid "069a0151-b380-5cfe-bc79-93245524b320" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056548} {:answer/id #uuid "13fd41af-5c6d-5dc2-b3df-814bcf97ea35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056549}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e1f0d44a-d8a6-5e77-99b2-1bbdefc5351c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056544}] :question/id #uuid "fe5f0f61-d46c-57e6-b1ba-ec9d07fb2f45" :question/math-academy-id "q-1355" :question/problem "If $a = ⟨ - 1, 0, 6⟩$ and $b = ⟨10, 2,-5⟩$, then $a \\cdot b =$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a057226-4563-56e2-8c25-e6d52f70db8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a057226-4563-56e2-8c25-e6d52f70db8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234756} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ebb2a22-14d9-5829-aa9d-41c29ede505f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235071}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e60be6b-04aa-5311-85b6-7c960267e903" :question/math-academy-id "q-168035" :question/problem "Find the dot product of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q\\cdot r=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The dot product of two vectors given in component form can be computed by summing up the products of corresponding components of vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & ={q}_{x}\\cdot {r}_{x}+{q}_{y}\\cdot {r}_{y}+{q}_{z}\\cdot {r}_{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom part 1, we have $q=⟨0,-3,2⟩$ and $r=⟨0,4,3⟩.$ Therefore, the formula for the dot product gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & =0\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0-12+6 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00754d46-0704-5773-b914-479b2780c54e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235797} {:answer/id #uuid "0b160a2e-ac6a-5783-b728-e3786b2e8ea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235873} {:answer/id #uuid "5e18d896-af8f-5c4e-a92e-a5e7a5d02427" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236408} {:answer/id #uuid "aa42023a-fee9-57d2-8160-bb0856641f36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236893} {:answer/id #uuid "fd10e16a-4040-5c60-bbca-1fcbbc9e602c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b160a2e-ac6a-5783-b728-e3786b2e8ea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235873} :answer-field/id #uuid "2955f949-c61e-5c52-a7ce-dd2c578781b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237493}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "424bd239-6062-5739-8f7b-4979cfdd4107" :question/math-academy-id "q-101406" :question/problem "Let $p=⟨1,-2⟩$ and $q=⟨4,-1⟩.$ Find $p\\cdot q.$" :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4+2 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19f4fbac-4061-5f3d-9799-55a99d06ca9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266362} {:answer/id #uuid "399da875-0cc4-5b61-a973-cc4519bb7617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266651} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0c297e-304e-5779-afcf-cf59460c8afd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267252} {:answer/id #uuid "ad65bdc8-68c1-535f-a56b-c476a9c4b5af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267709} {:answer/id #uuid "f1057cc8-fca6-5ace-b14b-ab32a6cdb93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1057cc8-fca6-5ace-b14b-ab32a6cdb93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268287} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e32f98a-0b5b-5df5-ace1-4bb6116c03b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268508}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bd6a5391-fcf3-5a3e-bf4c-ad2c6e4a6452" :question/math-academy-id "q-1341" :question/problem "If $\\overset{\\to }{a}=⟨1,-2,4⟩$ and $\\overset{\\to }{b}=⟨11,4,-1⟩$, then $\\overset{\\to }{a}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{b}=$" :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{a}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{b} & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 11+(-2)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =11+(-8)+(-4) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "425e3407-b831-5dfb-8a4e-ab70c457a4ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "425e3407-b831-5dfb-8a4e-ab70c457a4ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297820} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcec9a87-0fd2-5ac6-945b-1c415bc62f4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299275}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18bcf01e-256b-5339-97ad-00f972b0c662" :question/math-academy-id "q-317910" :question/problem "If $a=⟨5,1⟩$ and $b=⟨2,4⟩,$ then $a\\cdot b=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10+4 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299658 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35fdb316-399f-5821-b5d4-b5ce24c7099e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35fdb316-399f-5821-b5d4-b5ce24c7099e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297769} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dca9ebc-819e-5579-86a0-5f4b732b025c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298684}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02b21351-2b17-5c15-a1fb-09ee1d2960d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-317911" :question/problem "If $u=⟨8,-2⟩$ and $v=⟨3,6⟩,$ then $u\\cdot v=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24-12 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Dot Product Using the General Formula"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059731 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059544 :question/id #uuid "dfc10727-c0d7-5b83-a4f6-afe3eb4831cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4324" :question/problem "Let $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ t\\end{aligned}]$. Given that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$, find the value of $t$." :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$ ($\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are perpendicular) if and only if $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot t \\\\  & =-8-10+t \\\\  & =t-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ t-18 & =0 \\\\ t & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8bff08bf-0035-5f05-9607-493b301e8717" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048187 :topic/math-academy-id 430 :topic/title "Solving Equations Using the Square Root Method"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050938 :topic/math-academy-id 243 :topic/title "Calculating the Dot Product Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae77e54a-32d3-50f9-90e1-d721c6912eb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057565} {:answer/id #uuid "bef01f32-2af6-504c-9185-33a340c040ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057566} {:answer/id #uuid "05f7dc59-7d31-5a4e-b1a7-5bcc62a410e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057567} {:answer/id #uuid "126b8159-3ed9-5704-855e-553385d3d53f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057568} {:answer/id #uuid "424479e4-1853-5168-afdd-f90066e0a09b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057569}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3a0be646-0391-52b4-8b5c-f114ed783be8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057564}] :question/id #uuid "02c9cfa7-4ae9-5705-8d7c-fd2022315d5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-19021" :question/problem "Let $u = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$. Given that $u⊥v$ and $x > 0$, find the value of $x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a55d62b6-5917-5302-bee6-928b3a17278b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057571} {:answer/id #uuid "007b9b4a-9aba-5d0b-8651-b268b0d7200b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057572} {:answer/id #uuid "536fbee0-344e-58b1-8307-db534e6334b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057573} {:answer/id #uuid "61891842-8ad9-52be-9016-cfbcb9079347" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057574} {:answer/id #uuid "74d0b8c7-fc2c-5232-a7ad-7e4fb33c6ae2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057575}] :answer-field/id #uuid "69413196-ca59-537c-b270-83f81dac5f78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057570}] :question/id #uuid "14310796-c50e-535f-830b-a7d5f462ade4" :question/math-academy-id "q-19022" :question/problem "What is the value of $x$ given that $a = ⟨x,-6x, 3⟩, b = ⟨x, 1, 3⟩$ and $a⊥b$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35170554-7491-5b34-9b67-ab6efae808e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236152} {:answer/id #uuid "49bebe95-7d8f-5363-8791-a41d117d2f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236287} {:answer/id #uuid "77b5df1a-8495-5220-8d4a-3d2d72b7ceae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236568} {:answer/id #uuid "84346316-be9d-55ce-ad43-19e661050d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236640} {:answer/id #uuid "9da633c8-52af-507c-8a35-a65c81ee25b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77b5df1a-8495-5220-8d4a-3d2d72b7ceae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236568} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f7b6300-7056-5f11-ba41-499cc6516307" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237521}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfd0ffab-79f2-5643-9530-8f55bce579c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-101417" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 2x\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u⊥v$ and $x<0$, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $u⊥v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-2)+2x\\cdot x \\\\  & =-18+2{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ -18+2{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =18 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $x<0.$ Therefore, $x=-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6896d0d5-0d79-5756-b49d-54e6544b747c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267074} {:answer/id #uuid "739434d2-a34f-51ba-85b2-ecb051fb40b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267159} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9709bd-77ac-5c62-901d-3e693169f7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267686} {:answer/id #uuid "d662411b-1715-5ff4-8a35-4927cc146fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268054} {:answer/id #uuid "d927e205-8536-566a-9f6c-22e1afa9f648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "739434d2-a34f-51ba-85b2-ecb051fb40b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267159} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6039b6c-4aa0-5bb3-9ed0-9729597efec4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268702}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "214450de-6c4e-5468-90b3-b289da0c12f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-1348" :question/problem "Let $p=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ n\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $p⊥q$, find the value of $n.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $p⊥q$ ($p$ and $q$ are perpendicular) if and only if $p\\cdot q=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 4+n\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =28-4n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 28-4n & =0 \\\\ 28 & =4n \\\\ n & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cdf7785-cbcd-5112-bc95-0ebbc936c864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285506} {:answer/id #uuid "6c3e8d51-22f5-56d9-bed9-0046f6689fee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285779} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2594eb-bee1-5bc9-9567-d9bdbbe0c102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286647} {:answer/id #uuid "cd97d40d-cba1-5ada-8396-a11d2d4f6bbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286658} {:answer/id #uuid "e137dd90-b672-5a36-ac92-f22334af1df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd97d40d-cba1-5ada-8396-a11d2d4f6bbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286658} :answer-field/id #uuid "126e0055-240c-57c8-bdd7-5831adf2287c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287177}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9064a6be-d660-5dcb-af2d-9691a386096a" :question/math-academy-id "q-19023" :question/problem "Let $g=[\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$ and $h=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ {r}^{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot {r}^{2}+(-6)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3{r}^{2}-{r}^{2}-12 \\\\  & =2{r}^{2}-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =6 \\\\ r & =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\sqrt{6}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299660 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "050de492-c23d-5e5a-9515-f5292836bf29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "050de492-c23d-5e5a-9515-f5292836bf29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297577} :answer-field/id #uuid "af74f5ad-0374-5f9e-bd30-ae2ff4e64785" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299231}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6840a760-5144-5da8-bd56-8faedecfd9c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-317932" :question/problem "If $c=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 2k \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ $d=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ and $c⊥d,$ then $k=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $c⊥d$ ($c$ and $d$ are perpendicular) if and only if $c\\cdot d=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & ={c}_{x}\\cdot {d}_{x}+{c}_{y}\\cdot {d}_{y}+{c}_{z}\\cdot {d}_{z} \\\\  & =k\\cdot (-3)+2k\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-3k+4k+8 \\\\  & =k+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & =0 \\\\ k+8 & =0 \\\\ k & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc42bda9-d3c0-5507-b933-0b2f39398215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc42bda9-d3c0-5507-b933-0b2f39398215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298373} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0941247-a978-51c6-9a76-00d8d070c636" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299169}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d22ee02b-54e6-511a-8cc5-59280c888981" :question/math-academy-id "q-317945" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2{x}^{2},-4⟩$ and $b=⟨8,4⟩.$ If $a⊥b$ and $x>0,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $a⊥b$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $a\\cdot b=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}\\cdot 8+(-4)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16{x}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ 16{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $x>0.$ Therefore, $x=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345278 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb6caf7-964e-584f-8548-449063ff8736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342474} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6655fa-a76a-596f-a2ad-fcfeda7271b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343014} {:answer/id #uuid "683aa6b1-adb6-5752-98f4-3a273931868b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343127} {:answer/id #uuid "78d230ed-b93e-5bce-ae61-1e6e00da2e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343280} {:answer/id #uuid "d7db328f-e4c7-567e-b319-dbb4a9fef103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7db328f-e4c7-567e-b319-dbb4a9fef103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344135} :answer-field/id #uuid "67145e24-54e9-57c2-bd15-3f132d50bd30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344667}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b9597aa-ca6f-577e-9d42-415936c8f19c" :question/math-academy-id "q-77152" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u⊥v$ and $a<0$, find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $u⊥v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y}+{u}_{z}\\cdot {v}_{z} \\\\  & =a\\cdot a+2\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={a}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =16 \\\\ a & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $a<0.$ Therefore, $a=-4.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given Two Perpendicular Vectors"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059736 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059545 :question/id #uuid "d2698dbf-dea6-5abb-970e-a3ace180e337" :question/math-academy-id "e-4341" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 0)i-(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))j+(3\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot (-7))k \\\\  & =-8i-13j-28k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-13,-28⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048146 :topic/math-academy-id 153 :topic/title "The Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060046 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aac8c206-b291-573d-ae2a-74259dfb0e6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 28,-19,-61⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056635} {:answer/id #uuid "ca53652c-eb08-5737-b6e1-44c670d816d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/ma