#edb/ref 17592186286241} {:answer/id #uuid "a78cf6fe-6959-5fd6-96cd-441cf7f5493b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a78cf6fe-6959-5fd6-96cd-441cf7f5493b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286315} :answer-field/id #uuid "aedfe451-3be4-545f-acac-1c1f5c95d11b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287509}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "418b906a-1baf-59eb-8935-edc0e9f8b503" :question/math-academy-id "q-19786" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨2,0,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{13}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(6x-8)j+(0-2)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-(6x-8),-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-(6x-8))^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36{x}^{2}-96x+64+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-96x+77}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\ \\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-96x+77} & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\ 36{x}^{2}-96x+77 & =13 \\\\ 36{x}^{2}-96x+64 & =0 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-24x+16 & =0 \\\\ (3x-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3x-4 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{4}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "384052f7-8479-5451-8826-ebad4be0b9cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236174} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ceb671-4df1-5711-99a6-e539d10040f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237068} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf06b23-9d73-58e3-96a2-bad6a11980c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237111} {:answer/id #uuid "d5aad3f9-96d0-5577-81a4-3ff8e34b23b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237166} {:answer/id #uuid "fd975286-7f8a-5f9b-80aa-d25b3f4ae72a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5ceb671-4df1-5711-99a6-e539d10040f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237068} :answer-field/id #uuid "3adb5c55-83aa-583d-aebb-812163c6902d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237517}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1839cab9-bd67-5688-9a2a-104436b124ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-103540" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,3,2⟩$, $b=⟨x,1,-1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{93}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 2 \\\\ x & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 2 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ x & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-3-2)i-(-2x-2x)j+(2x-3x)k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+16{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ \\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25} & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ 17{x}^{2}+25 & =93 \\\\ 17{x}^{2} & =68 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c05b61-7dc6-53f0-8eed-7743ecb92787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235813} {:answer/id #uuid "837899b1-cc2e-59cf-a23a-35f2ed00b6cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236639} {:answer/id #uuid "90b48184-136a-57ff-a6c6-8aa6ad551689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236738} {:answer/id #uuid "9673d4c2-53f4-5a56-9462-97e02a7c3a6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236772} {:answer/id #uuid "b4be8d8f-4a66-536f-b059-008317284b6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "837899b1-cc2e-59cf-a23a-35f2ed00b6cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236639} :answer-field/id #uuid "452b7748-b2b6-53f6-b879-d5ef2699fbff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237527}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a06523df-238f-57e5-936a-f93168e3e76d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103541" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-3,2,0⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-4,2x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{77}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4x-0)i-(-6x-0)j+(12-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4x,6x,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}+(6x)^{2}+(8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52{x}^{2}+64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{77} \\\\ \\sqrt{52{x}^{2}+64} & =\\sqrt{77} \\\\ 52{x}^{2}+64 & =77 \\\\ 52{x}^{2} & =13 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238018 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1042b2b0-48dd-582d-b30e-d64f5e68e655" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235904} {:answer/id #uuid "531f08ba-c26d-5ffb-b31b-76da888b8b0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236345} {:answer/id #uuid "95806bed-6677-52d1-86f0-a9c3b398a75a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{3},3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236766} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc5b9af-1b07-5068-bffd-2500e6a28cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237209} {:answer/id #uuid "eb84ec79-c885-5346-994b-a3ef1e3618cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1042b2b0-48dd-582d-b30e-d64f5e68e655" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235904} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fd051b8-cfd0-500d-b748-e9e245e480d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237585}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98e8a01d-ba49-5e10-81ec-e89893b65589" :question/math-academy-id "q-103542" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-1,2x,3⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-x,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{355}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 2x & 3 \\\\ 2 & -x & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2x \\\\ 2 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2x+3x)i-(-1-6)j+(x-4x)k \\\\  & =⟨5x,7,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}+49+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ \\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49} & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ 34{x}^{2}+49 & =355 \\\\ 34{x}^{2} & =306 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2396dede-1b82-5a2a-aa5a-3223ea475b72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4,\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236045} {:answer/id #uuid "5d433363-5f65-5914-a92b-e08e2d8de45b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-10,\\,-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236404} {:answer/id #uuid "acd9a719-7f3e-5a4e-b249-7cef823b6db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,\\,10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236917} {:answer/id #uuid "b8694282-defb-545d-a22d-31c29f015388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236996} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4c7f2d-5e99-56fc-9df8-7f1922ff63db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d433363-5f65-5914-a92b-e08e2d8de45b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-10,\\,-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236404} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c1bd1fc-a71d-5a23-a644-e9a570aa5b28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237580}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fc2ecbe1-ea04-53ab-bfa6-277a8ca05a39" :question/math-academy-id "q-103547" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨4,x,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-2,3,0⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{181}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & x & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & x \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0-9)i-(0+6)j+(12+2x)k \\\\  & =⟨-9,-6,12+2x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-9)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(12+2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81+36+144+48x+4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{261+48x+4{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{181} \\\\ \\sqrt{261+48x+4{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{181} \\\\ 261+48x+4{x}^{2} & =181 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+48x+80 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+12x+20 & =0 \\\\ (x+10)(x+2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-10,\\,-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fc2a099-bf95-50e1-b9c3-7330e50dafc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236020} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7bbb8f-90eb-5b64-af7c-61e67a66ae8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236104} {:answer/id #uuid "422c528b-268c-59a9-aa08-17ee3b5fb935" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236239} {:answer/id #uuid "457328c4-1a16-5b0d-8e61-d406b9702bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236264} {:answer/id #uuid "a01206ba-e5ec-539f-b8df-b8f8806d9468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "422c528b-268c-59a9-aa08-17ee3b5fb935" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236239} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b389ae5-8e6c-5abf-8392-283e3441d1c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237562}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9e02b899-797e-55fb-bf98-84a59903fc4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103549" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,3,4⟩,$ $b=⟨-1,-x,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{221}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -x & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -x & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(6+4x)i-(0+4)j+(0+3)k \\\\  & =⟨6+4x,-4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(6+4x)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+48x+16{x}^{2}+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{61+48x+16{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{221} \\\\ \\sqrt{61+48x+16{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{221} \\\\ 61+48x+16{x}^{2} & =221 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}+48x-160 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3x-10 & =0 \\\\ (x+5)(x-2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-5,\\,2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238024 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "139a429e-ade1-501e-b65f-dac725fd7e68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235932} {:answer/id #uuid "16719391-8dec-5e82-b401-93ca0e8487a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235956} {:answer/id #uuid "49cb3763-a9d5-5bb5-9b6a-9d363519fada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236290} {:answer/id #uuid "a927a9d7-e41d-58d1-9c3c-54f2ab45e590" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236882} {:answer/id #uuid "aa115508-6b4c-591b-b7d1-64700634a6e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a927a9d7-e41d-58d1-9c3c-54f2ab45e590" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236882} :answer-field/id #uuid "cde4e8a4-64c8-57b9-ac27-5d4fb7853626" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237711}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "357e8faf-9623-5ade-84da-303c65f27082" :question/math-academy-id "q-103552" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,-2,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-2,1,-2x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{53}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4x-3)i-(0+6)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4x-3,-6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+9+36+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+61}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{53} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-24x+61} & =\\sqrt{53} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-24x+61 & =53 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-24x+8 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x+1 & =0 \\\\ (2x-1)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2},\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287959 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a5faf31-a027-54f6-893d-fa34e1417998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285338} {:answer/id #uuid "493b1d43-5539-572e-ab49-36f99c567690" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285461} {:answer/id #uuid "55ef5465-6e15-524b-ae92-901d3537d994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285578} {:answer/id #uuid "e52f12ca-7b96-5ce8-9839-d0542ceca526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286885} {:answer/id #uuid "fdeb9f25-fa5b-5fd4-a92b-3143e29bce7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55ef5465-6e15-524b-ae92-901d3537d994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285578} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f1a7ec0-67e0-5864-a6a8-3f8391794ca7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287324}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "421f4045-e8df-5b08-89fb-dae822bc3289" :question/math-academy-id "q-19785" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨2x,5,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{393}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2x & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 2x & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 2x & 5\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4-15)i-(2x-6x)j+(5x-4x)k \\\\  & =⟨-11,4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-11)^{2}+(4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{121+16{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+121}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{393} \\\\ \\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+121} & =\\sqrt{393} \\\\ 17{x}^{2}+121 & =393 \\\\ 17{x}^{2} & =272 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b70cc5e3-ce9b-587a-856e-446f9654bd7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b70cc5e3-ce9b-587a-856e-446f9654bd7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291425} :answer-field/id #uuid "088b5a0c-ad44-5fc4-9428-330d1ccbe936" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5deb2570-5a15-57c0-8f85-5aad6b606da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5deb2570-5a15-57c0-8f85-5aad6b606da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291033} :answer-field/id #uuid "18dbf2c9-5d0b-5815-b5f5-495a6394fcc0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291829}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c72f4aa-ab5b-5b58-b34b-802301025714" :question/math-academy-id "q-275278" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-2x,3,5⟩,$ $b=⟨2x,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{909}.$ Then, in **ascending order**,  the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2x & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2x & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2x & 5 \\\\ 2x & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2x & 3 \\\\ 2x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(-2x-10x)j+(0-6x)k \\\\  & =⟨3,12x,-6x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(12x)^{2}+(-6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+144{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{909} \\\\ \\sqrt{180{x}^{2}+9} & =\\sqrt{909} \\\\ 180{x}^{2}+9 & =909 \\\\ 180{x}^{2} & =900 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\sqrt{5},$ $x=\\sqrt{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e708bcc-57d6-5c73-b04e-955486a1bf34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e708bcc-57d6-5c73-b04e-955486a1bf34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293557} :answer-field/id #uuid "48faf064-a2f6-51ea-9045-dffbdc7bd32a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294187}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7575e8a2-e97b-54b4-80f9-81b1c7ceb471" :question/math-academy-id "q-278839" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,2,1⟩,$ $b=⟨2,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{20}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(x-2)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨2,2-x,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2-x)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4-4x+{x}^{2}+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-4x+24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-4x+24} & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+24 & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+4 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6399e3b8-ff34-55fc-a47f-71dc471f219c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6399e3b8-ff34-55fc-a47f-71dc471f219c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293339} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fd515cd-c214-5167-b7ba-c4def2042247" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294272} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d675942-4fa7-5d27-8386-58830bed7ca6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d675942-4fa7-5d27-8386-58830bed7ca6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293390} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3f82250-dec1-5957-8cd9-d5e3812caae9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294676}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3a69df9-3422-55c4-b6e2-d44c3f81e8dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-282260" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,3,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-2x,0,4⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{280}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2x & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ -2x & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -2x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(12-0)i-(8x+2x)j+(0+6x)k \\\\  & =⟨12,-10x,6x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+(-10x)^{2}+(6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+100{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ \\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144} & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ 136{x}^{2}+144 & =280 \\\\ 136{x}^{2} & =136 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-1,$ $x=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c089ac0-6345-5a8c-b62f-0ed057920e41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c089ac0-6345-5a8c-b62f-0ed057920e41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293300} :answer-field/id #uuid "07bd3ca9-b08b-5bba-b233-e5435a9a2640" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "593dad82-9cf7-57f0-a8f9-1d4350843ab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "593dad82-9cf7-57f0-a8f9-1d4350843ab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293290} :answer-field/id #uuid "2929fa13-2cfd-51a7-8f49-b45196662e2c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294067}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e10f888-66d4-5375-8f79-b8da98cf5664" :question/math-academy-id "q-282261" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,0,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,2,0⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{29}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 0 & 1 \\\\ -x & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0-2)i-(0+x)j+(2x+0)k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-x,2x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+{x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{29} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{x}^{2}+4} & =\\sqrt{29} \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4 & =29 \\\\ 5{x}^{2} & =25 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\sqrt{5},$ $x=\\sqrt{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fe042d9-f712-540a-9a31-4c3f6a49c2a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fe042d9-f712-540a-9a31-4c3f6a49c2a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293064} :answer-field/id #uuid "472a2680-c3e4-5a4b-bf63-8a3b7676904d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8df1edb2-60a1-5e25-a033-c22d6600a279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8df1edb2-60a1-5e25-a033-c22d6600a279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293481} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecc407dd-1a3f-56e7-be3e-e7615f20ae61" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294760}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "999eb6f6-f5c6-519d-9ac7-4875fbf986b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-282262" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,3,0⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{49}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 3 & 0 \\\\ -x & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(x+0)j+(0+3x)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-x,3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ 10{x}^{2}+9 & =49 \\\\ 10{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2,$ $x=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40d647f4-bc4e-5f76-acc3-d8205ef31c67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40d647f4-bc4e-5f76-acc3-d8205ef31c67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293195} :answer-field/id #uuid "8623129c-f6e8-53ae-bd31-d59d37637d0c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294406}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59e9fba3-4db6-5c48-86ed-2af0a557b731" :question/math-academy-id "q-282269" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,1,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{10}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(3x-1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨3,1-3x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(1-3x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+(9{x}^{2}-6x+1)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+11} & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-6x+11 & =10 \\\\ (3x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63fe025d-813b-5f9a-9c06-c0556ddb9547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63fe025d-813b-5f9a-9c06-c0556ddb9547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293343} :answer-field/id #uuid "c20c34ca-4ea2-51bf-9889-6f3124593e13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294618}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f7de1193-053f-5234-9520-07973769fe4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-282270" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,1,2⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{5}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2x-2)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨2,2-2x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2-2x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(4{x}^{2}-8x+4)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+9 & =5 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+4 & =0 \\\\ (2x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09cb1d18-d1e0-565d-bb78-b6a4658bbe13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09cb1d18-d1e0-565d-bb78-b6a4658bbe13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292974} :answer-field/id #uuid "03c55d87-7acb-572f-811d-7189f6ef9993" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b32daaa-10cc-5583-9726-450366961c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b32daaa-10cc-5583-9726-450366961c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292978} :answer-field/id #uuid "508dcba7-f96e-5b1d-99d9-43b1a4ce626c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294216}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe9d7249-168a-5810-85b9-89bad6dafc21" :question/math-academy-id "q-282276" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,4,5⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{33}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4-0)i-(x-5)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4,5-x,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(5-x)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+(25-10x+{x}^{2})+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+57}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{33} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+57} & =\\sqrt{33} \\\\ {x}^{2}-10x+57 & =33 \\\\ {x}^{2}-10x+24 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =4,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=4,$ $x=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44a3a765-13c2-5f3d-89c8-752a0cc1e107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44a3a765-13c2-5f3d-89c8-752a0cc1e107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293214} :answer-field/id #uuid "c018ffe1-59c2-5c29-85ed-cac2b8dc9161" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294612} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e6e2225-14bc-5817-b2b0-9fa7c511b22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e6e2225-14bc-5817-b2b0-9fa7c511b22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293441} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9a690fb-f7f4-52fd-8017-428f88655eec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294695}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d9b76997-cb19-548e-a5c8-ac57874f667e" :question/math-academy-id "q-282278" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{157}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(4x-12)j+(0-3)k \\\\  & =⟨2,12-4x,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(12-4x)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(144-96x+16{x}^{2})+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157} & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x+157 & =157 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x & =0 \\\\ 16x(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45ba9575-4116-5da1-9d13-75fddafe1880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342813} {:answer/id #uuid "56459a3a-433a-5d89-a00c-d2db7f4af24d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342956} {:answer/id #uuid "b56ab6d7-6374-51b8-a73a-573a9c6d25f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343828} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d83a2c-baf4-5473-8f83-d89b478ba56a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344213} {:answer/id #uuid "ebf2aebc-fe9e-54f8-8ae7-fef78f976954" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56459a3a-433a-5d89-a00c-d2db7f4af24d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342956} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a05ee8c-a6f2-5705-ac77-f7c2d74908f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344565}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c996c916-6d56-55b9-8504-9c0842874c89" :question/math-academy-id "q-77427" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,x,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,-x,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=10.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3x+x)i-(6-1)j+(-2x-x)k \\\\  & =⟨4x,-5,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+25+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =10 \\\\ \\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)} & =10 \\\\ 25({x}^{2}+1) & =100 \\\\ {x}^{2}+1 & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345296 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00fa6337-ab0d-5160-a611-2ddc8da0cf63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342253} {:answer/id #uuid "09269469-cfd9-5d57-8d8b-42fdb071211c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342313} {:answer/id #uuid "23a6c0cd-5de2-535e-b93e-c6aa000f9907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342534} {:answer/id #uuid "51e0ea9c-50b6-5b70-92d8-61c5f756d8a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342915} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c26781-a599-5f95-bd31-c91372b3df28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23a6c0cd-5de2-535e-b93e-c6aa000f9907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342534} :answer-field/id #uuid "0083fa75-a1b0-5b25-a910-a26f765c9e50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344494}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d7c9e319-7861-5d4f-b23a-d86c9fbc5eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-77429" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,0,-4⟩,$ $b=⟨-1,1,2x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=2\\sqrt{5}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 2x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0+4)i-(4x-4)j+(2-0)k \\\\  & =⟨4,-4x+4,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4x+4)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16{x}^{2}-32x+16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-32x+36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-32x+36} & =2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-32x+36 & =20 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-32x+16 & =0 \\\\ 16({x}^{2}-2x+1) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+1 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c6f3048-c777-5c58-90fe-219a1e995028" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366200} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd8a995-6178-5f31-b28a-0d7684d7534e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366201} {:answer/id #uuid "609d7569-0efb-5912-8d7e-ef9c759ef0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366202} {:answer/id #uuid "1416b5a2-f91d-5f4c-bd8d-6c79bf571891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\,6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366203} {:answer/id #uuid "3aafa1d8-531c-5437-99ef-3fa345bb7b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2,\\,6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3aafa1d8-531c-5437-99ef-3fa345bb7b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2,\\,6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366204} :answer-field/id #uuid "b200d0bf-bed1-5cf6-8f1e-f47e978d20c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366199}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fcbb93c0-afa4-55f5-929f-c8cc83bbc10c" :question/math-academy-id "q-69776" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨4,2,-1⟩$, $b=⟨x,2,-1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{20}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ x & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ x & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-2+2)i-(-4+x)j+(8-2x)k \\\\  & =⟨0,4-x,8-2x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(4-x)^{2}+(8-2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16-8x+{x}^{2}+64-32x+4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}-40x+80}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{x}^{2}-40x+80} & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-40x+80 & =20 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-40x+60 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-8x+12 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)(x-6) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=2,\\,6.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}]}
